  "teachingInsertions": {
    "kanji/絹.md": [
      "- Complete comparison entries also record きぎぬ for [絡](絡.md), thread senses for [緒](緒.md) and [線](線.md), a Buddhist noose for [索](索.md), and a snare sense of くくり for [括](括.md). These positive secondary senses motivate additional direct guards; they do not make all entwining, rope or tying synonymous with silk.\n"
    ],
    "kanji/虹.md": [
      "- [輪](輪.md), ring, [円](円.md), circle, and [光](光.md), light, guard broad descriptive labels: [日本大百科全書](https://kotobank.jp/word/虹) describes a rainbow as a coloured ring of light. This is not unrestricted lexical synonymy or a demonstrated collision in the three curated meaning options.\n",
      "- Independently attested criticism/censure senses of [批](批.md) and [劾](劾.md), dispute/debate senses of [議](議.md) and [談](談.md), attack for [撃](撃.md), disorder for [騒](騒.md) and [動](動.md), blame for [罪](罪.md), coercive pressure for [圧](圧.md), and opposition for [抗](抗.md), [反](反.md), [対](対.md) and [抵](抵.md) motivate further conservative direct guards around that unresolved range.\n",
      "- [曲](曲.md) also has a noun sense of a curve; [器](器.md), [盆](盆.md) and [盤](盤.md) have vessel/dish senses, while [缶](缶.md) has a broad container label. Their guards protect broad shape or historical oil-dish choices, not a claim that music, boards or every kind of can means rainbow.\n"
    ]
  },
